lisa-design:
- Observe reads only comments.totalCount: with no marker read-back, comment bodies and the ObserveComments follow-up pages have no reader, so Observe reads no untrusted comment text and makes fewer calls. The recorded GraphQL fixtures keep only the count.
- Project keeps reading the App's own markers (markers, mine, othersOwn), moved from observe.go to project.go; TestProjectReadsOnlyItsMarkers carries over Observe's golden marker cases (forged, reviewer App, deleted account, v2, duplicate, past the first page).
- The fake keeps per-object projections in its own map (marks) for ProjectCall.Changed and exposes them via ProjectionsOn(ref); Seed of an object clears them (as replacing the Observation did).
- Webhook refusals use provider.WriteProblem (FND), since the fake cannot import internal/server (server's package tests import the fake: cycle). The GitHub adapter passes internal/server's Code* constants; the fake uses the same strings as literals. 5xx carry no detail, as the server's errorHandler.
- github.Conn drops the orgs field: Provider scope.orgs bounded only List. The contract field stays (contracts in their own PR); raised for triage.
- github-provider.md renames its section to "Observe and projection" with an explicit <a id="observe-list-and-projection"> so 02-architecture.md's link keeps working without editing a file outside GH/FND.
